---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
---
<Tunnel title="Follow The Cable | Save My Gig!" status="No_Sound · Master" red>
  <div class="step-label">Out of the mixer</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Follow the cable out</h2>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Reseat the master output cables, both ends.</li>
    <li>Swap the master pair for the <strong>booth output</strong> pair if there is one.</li>
    <li>Amps powered? In most venues the rack is not in the booth, so this is usually a question for someone else, not a thing you check.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- The amp rack is normally locked or out of the room, so "look at the amp"
       was an instruction the DJ often cannot carry out. What they actually need
       is the sentence that gets someone else to check it, and the evidence that
       makes the tech take it seriously. -->
  <details class="move-more" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">
    <summary>Words for whoever runs the room</summary>
    <p>
      <strong>"My master is up and the meters are moving. Can someone confirm
      the amps are powered?"</strong>
      <br /><br />
      Naming the meters matters. It is the difference between a request they
      have to investigate and one they can answer immediately.
    </p>
  </details>

  <p class="question">Sound now?</p>

  <Choice step="ns_master2"
    a={{ href: '/saved?path=no_sound&branch=cable', label: 'YES, IT PLAYS', event: 'outcome_reached', data: { outcome: 'saved', path: 'no_sound' } }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/no-sound/house', label: 'NO, STILL SILENT' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
